<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Free Nelson Mandela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1984">1984</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nelson Mandela</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>&quot;, known in some versions as &quot;Free Nelson Mandela&quot;, was written by the British musician Jerry Dammers and recorded by the band the Special A.K.A., with Stan Campbell singing lead. Dammers said he knew very little about Mandela until he went to an anti-apartheid concert in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1983, which gave him the idea for the song.</p></div>
